WEBVTT

00:07.215 --> 00:10.677
You're… Erasure Hero.

00:10.760 --> 00:12.262
Eraser Head.

00:12.345 --> 00:15.056
Hero? Do you know who that is?

00:15.807 --> 00:19.936
I'm off-duty today. So, I'm just
a regular citizen with good intentions.

00:20.020 --> 00:23.148
We're alike. Since I'm the same.

00:25.150 --> 00:28.570
Could it be that we're being treated
as Villains?

00:28.653 --> 00:31.322
What? I have nothing
to do with that old man.

00:31.406 --> 00:32.741
I'm not either!

00:44.335 --> 00:46.296
He started fighting with a Hero!

00:46.379 --> 00:48.548
That old man is definitely crazy!

00:56.639 --> 00:59.809
<i>He's the type that bulldozes</i>
<i>using his durability enhancing Quirk.</i>

01:00.477 --> 01:02.520
<i>Putting my energy into this fight</i>

01:03.772 --> 01:05.106
<i>is not logical.</i>

01:19.913 --> 01:21.414
<i>Erasure has no effect on him.</i>

01:24.584 --> 01:25.960
<i>I understand it now.</i>

01:26.961 --> 01:30.381
<i>This guy… This guy's Quirk is…</i>

03:01.556 --> 03:03.224
VIGILANTE
A CRIME PREVENTION ORGANIZATION

03:03.308 --> 03:05.059
THAT OPERATES OUTSIDE OF LEGAL PROCEDURES
A VIGILANTE GROUP

03:05.143 --> 03:06.978
ALSO REFERS TO MEMBERS OF VIGILANTE GROUPS
WHO ENCOURAGE VIGILANTISM

03:13.776 --> 03:16.029
What are we supposed to do now?

03:21.659 --> 03:23.995
Oh, that guy…

03:24.787 --> 03:27.373
I feel like I've seen
that silhouette before.

03:28.041 --> 03:30.752
That's right. When I was searching
a while ago…

03:32.587 --> 03:34.339
I knew it.

03:34.422 --> 03:37.425
He's always in the pictures
related to Villain incidents.

03:37.508 --> 03:40.303
Koichi, I think he knows something.

03:42.639 --> 03:45.016
Look, he's running! He's suspicious!

03:46.184 --> 03:47.352
Chase him, Koichi!

03:49.520 --> 03:51.564
Please stop!

03:52.857 --> 03:55.109
Can I at least check your tongue?

04:01.866 --> 04:05.245
Let's settle last night's
unfinished business.

04:16.839 --> 04:19.842
What's wrong? Giving up already?

04:22.136 --> 04:25.473
I'm sorry. It was my misunderstanding.

04:26.349 --> 04:28.768
As long as there's no
"improper use of Quirks",

04:29.769 --> 04:32.397
I have no reason to capture you.

04:33.982 --> 04:36.109
EYE DROPS

04:38.361 --> 04:41.030
I thought you were some sort of a Villain.

04:42.573 --> 04:44.242
I get mistaken for them a lot.

04:44.325 --> 04:46.786
I see. I'm sorry.

04:48.454 --> 04:50.456
<i>He's so brazen…</i>

04:51.040 --> 04:53.584
<i>But at this moment,</i>
<i>I can't charge him with anything.</i>

04:56.004 --> 04:58.798
<i>Erasure had no effect on him.</i>

04:58.881 --> 05:01.467
<i>Which means he's Quirkless.</i>

05:02.135 --> 05:04.095
<i>He's just a burly old man.</i>

05:07.098 --> 05:10.893
<i>But it doesn't change the fact</i>
<i>that he's a suspicious individual.</i>

05:11.686 --> 05:14.605
<i>I'll report it to the police just in case.</i>

05:18.985 --> 05:20.611
Villains!

05:20.695 --> 05:22.363
Villains have appeared!

05:23.781 --> 05:26.993
Running away is the only thing
you're good at, huh?

05:29.078 --> 05:30.913
Try to dodge this!

05:41.049 --> 05:42.425
Oops.

05:42.508 --> 05:44.594
I'm here, on this side.

05:46.387 --> 05:47.555
<i>Oh crap!</i>

05:49.307 --> 05:53.436
At the same time, I'm here too!

06:02.862 --> 06:05.323
Master! Knuckle-san!

06:05.948 --> 06:07.116
Where's the girl?

06:07.700 --> 06:09.577
She's chasing that office worker.

06:11.370 --> 06:13.915
I won't let you get away!

06:18.878 --> 06:21.339
What is this? I can't move.

06:23.132 --> 06:25.468
Dealing with someone like you.

06:26.844 --> 06:28.721
Now that's a job for Heroes.

06:30.348 --> 06:31.974
Although I'm off-duty today.

06:35.394 --> 06:37.814
Stop right there!

06:39.190 --> 06:41.192
I told you to stop!

06:51.828 --> 06:53.621
My dolls fell out again.

06:56.999 --> 07:00.002
My dolls…

07:47.842 --> 07:51.262
-It's huge!
-It's a Colossal Villain.

07:51.762 --> 07:55.099
-Run!
-Wow! I've got to take a picture!

07:55.183 --> 07:56.893
Idiot! Call the Heroes!

07:56.976 --> 07:59.854
QUIRK
PLAYTIME

08:26.714 --> 08:27.673
Master!

08:32.929 --> 08:34.430
Pop!

08:34.514 --> 08:37.308
<i>Her Quirk is Leap.</i>

08:38.392 --> 08:39.727
<i>She has no footing to leap from.</i>

08:40.520 --> 08:43.814
<i>At this rate, she'll slam into the ground!</i>

08:47.902 --> 08:49.070
<i>A while ago, she asked me…</i>

08:49.987 --> 08:52.573
Why are you helping out this guy?

08:53.866 --> 08:55.159
<i>The answer</i>

08:56.077 --> 08:57.286
<i>to her question is…</i>

09:00.873 --> 09:02.291
<i>Because I want to be a Hero.</i>

09:05.086 --> 09:07.255
<i>I know I don't have a chance</i>
<i>at becoming a Pro Hero.</i>

09:08.005 --> 09:09.840
<i>I know that already. But…</i>

09:11.384 --> 09:12.802
<i>Even if just for one moment…</i>

09:14.345 --> 09:16.013
<i>I want to soar across the sky too!</i>

09:20.059 --> 09:20.977
Koichi!

09:22.270 --> 09:23.896
Leap!

09:28.526 --> 09:29.694
Koichi!

09:49.171 --> 09:50.006
I'm alive.

09:50.965 --> 09:52.300
Koichi!

09:55.970 --> 09:57.096
He's coming!

10:14.488 --> 10:17.450
Naturally, he will shrink
once I erase his Gigantification Quirk.

10:18.326 --> 10:21.787
It's only logical to apprehend him
after that.

10:30.921 --> 10:34.550
I guess I'll say thank you
for your cooperation.

10:35.176 --> 10:38.179
I told you that I'm also
a citizen with good intentions.

10:38.929 --> 10:41.891
It's my duty to cooperate with Heroes.

10:42.475 --> 10:46.604
Although playing make-believe Heroes
is causing more danger than doing good.

10:48.272 --> 10:51.275
We're doing things
that Pro Heroes can't do.

10:51.776 --> 10:53.235
Things we can't do?

10:53.736 --> 10:57.406
The gigantic Villain
and other delinquents we saw today.

10:58.115 --> 11:01.410
We can beat them up before
they do anything bad.

11:01.952 --> 11:05.706
Whoa, if you beat up people
who haven't done anything,

11:05.790 --> 11:07.208
that itself is a crime.

11:07.792 --> 11:09.543
If we follow that reasoning,

11:09.627 --> 11:14.548
you'll only be able to arrest us
"after we get the job done". Right?

11:14.632 --> 11:17.760
A willful offender who'll do whatever
he thinks is right, huh?

11:18.886 --> 11:21.555
You've got a really bad attitude.

11:22.473 --> 11:23.891
I get that a lot.

11:29.355 --> 11:31.774
Koichi. Are you all right?

11:32.358 --> 11:34.652
Yeah. I'm just a little tired.

11:35.611 --> 11:37.988
It's a good lesson not to do something
you're not cut out to do.

11:38.781 --> 11:41.242
Acting like a Hero and trying
to fight a big battle.

11:41.992 --> 11:45.955
It's just not who I am, you know.
I ended up falling too.

11:47.581 --> 11:48.791
I thought I was going to die.

11:49.291 --> 11:53.379
Hey, that kind of stuff is so annoying!

11:54.296 --> 11:58.342
Are you trying to make excuses
or be humble or something?

11:58.426 --> 12:00.177
It's useless so you should stop.

12:02.430 --> 12:06.142
I wanted to thank you, but you're
annoying, so I won't say it.

12:07.393 --> 12:11.439
Koichi, let me tell you why you fell.

12:13.441 --> 12:17.862
It's because you were in the air.
You just have to figure out how to land.

12:18.904 --> 12:22.324
I applaud you for imitating me
and falling into a pile of garbage.

12:22.408 --> 12:26.203
But there are lots of other things
you still need to learn.

12:26.287 --> 12:29.248
Like I said, I don't plan on being
your apprentice.

12:29.874 --> 12:32.501
You called me Master a while ago.

12:32.585 --> 12:36.881
Well… That was a slip of the tongue.
It was easier than Knuckle-san.

12:36.964 --> 12:38.966
Then even more so.

12:39.967 --> 12:43.179
"Slip of the tongue",
or impromptu words and actions,

12:43.262 --> 12:45.890
reveal your true feelings.

12:46.557 --> 12:48.309
Face the truth, Hero Wannabe.

12:50.561 --> 12:51.687
Well…

12:51.770 --> 12:55.441
That reasoning is a bit forced, isn't it?

13:05.409 --> 13:08.078
<i>Yeah, it's a fight.</i>

13:08.162 --> 13:11.081
-What the hell?
-Wanna die?

13:11.165 --> 13:13.042
Don't underestimate me,
you country bumpkin!

13:13.125 --> 13:16.504
What did you say? Better not choke
on your own spit, you moron!

13:21.383 --> 13:24.512
They're using their Quirks
and wreaking havoc by the train station.

13:24.595 --> 13:27.097
They're wearing uniforms,
so maybe they're high schoolers?

13:28.140 --> 13:28.974
You bastard!

13:29.058 --> 13:30.392
Which middle school are you from?

13:30.476 --> 13:32.186
Name your middle school first!

13:32.770 --> 13:34.438
Nope, they're middle schoolers.

13:35.022 --> 13:36.774
Roger. I'll head there right away.

13:38.108 --> 13:40.945
Koichi. I'll give you something useful.

13:41.028 --> 13:41.904
Useful?

13:42.488 --> 13:44.031
<i>Protective gear for motorcyclists</i>

13:44.615 --> 13:47.117
<i>and protective body gear to wear</i>
<i>under your hoodie.</i>

13:47.660 --> 13:50.454
<i>Now you can increase</i>
<i>your speed to your heart's content.</i>

13:54.083 --> 13:55.709
Stop fighting!

13:59.630 --> 14:02.466
Whoa… whoa…

14:03.092 --> 14:05.886
-Who are you?
-Are you all right?

14:07.972 --> 14:09.682
That didn't hurt at all.

14:11.559 --> 14:13.978
Why'd you barge in here all of a sudden?

14:14.562 --> 14:18.190
You'll be underestimated by criminals
if your name is Nice Guy.

14:18.274 --> 14:20.693
You need a new name.

14:23.195 --> 14:24.363
Want to know who I am?

14:26.782 --> 14:27.908
I am…

14:33.080 --> 14:35.457
The man with a scent of mystery.

14:35.541 --> 14:37.126
The Crawler!

14:39.962 --> 14:42.006
What are you saying? You're Nice Guy.

14:42.089 --> 14:43.007
Right?

14:44.133 --> 14:45.968
Oh, the one who's always picking up trash.

14:46.051 --> 14:47.928
You're so impressive.

14:48.012 --> 14:51.849
No, I have changed from Nice Guy
to The Crawler.

14:51.932 --> 14:53.017
The Squalor?

14:53.100 --> 14:55.728
No, no, it's not The Squalor.

14:55.811 --> 14:58.522
The Crawler!

14:58.606 --> 15:00.816
The way you rolled your tongue
is irritating.

15:01.483 --> 15:05.070
Anway, stop fighting. Say no to violence.

15:05.154 --> 15:08.198
-What?
-Why are you bossing us around?

15:08.282 --> 15:11.577
What was that for? Stop that.

15:11.660 --> 15:13.871
My protective gear is working.
It doesn't hurt at all!

15:16.040 --> 15:18.709
You bastard!

15:18.792 --> 15:20.085
My eyes!

15:20.169 --> 15:22.796
Don't get carried away, Nice Guy!

15:22.880 --> 15:24.298
I'm The Crawler!

15:24.381 --> 15:27.217
Just stick to cleaning like you always do.

15:27.301 --> 15:29.553
Sure, I don't mind cleaning.

15:33.724 --> 15:35.851
I'll clean up scums like you guys.

15:36.352 --> 15:37.269
Master!

15:38.520 --> 15:39.813
Who's this geezer?

15:39.897 --> 15:43.192
Hey brats. I'm going
to punch you guys right now.

15:43.734 --> 15:46.153
Then I need to confirm something.

15:46.236 --> 15:51.158
Stop! You don't need to punch them!
Why do you have to start with violence?

15:51.909 --> 15:55.871
Beating them up gets the job done faster.
Above all, it's refreshing.

15:55.955 --> 15:58.374
You can't hit people
just to feel refreshed.

16:00.376 --> 16:01.418
Why?

16:01.502 --> 16:02.586
You're asking why?

16:02.670 --> 16:05.339
-Whoa.
-Are they serious?

16:06.298 --> 16:07.341
Oh geez, they're a mess.

16:09.718 --> 16:12.304
Hey. Can I have a minute?

16:12.388 --> 16:13.555
Pop Step!

16:13.639 --> 16:16.767
I'm always watching your videos online.

16:16.850 --> 16:18.852
Me too. I always hit the "like" button.

16:18.936 --> 16:20.896
Thank you. Want my autograph?

16:20.980 --> 16:22.815
-Yes, please!
-Yes, please!

16:22.898 --> 16:25.067
Those guys

16:25.150 --> 16:29.196
aren't exactly bad people,
but they're not decent people either.

16:29.279 --> 16:31.073
I'm decent.

16:31.156 --> 16:32.574
I wonder.

16:37.496 --> 16:39.456
-Villain!
-A Villain has appeared!

16:39.540 --> 16:42.167
I'm hard. I'm really hard.

16:42.251 --> 16:46.422
I'm invincible.
I'm harder than a building!

16:48.424 --> 16:49.925
The baby!

17:00.269 --> 17:01.478
Safe and sound.

17:01.562 --> 17:02.688
All right!

17:08.235 --> 17:09.611
Whoa, he's super strong.

17:09.695 --> 17:11.155
Call the Heroes! The Heroes!

17:12.406 --> 17:15.034
No one can hurt me!

17:16.452 --> 17:17.870
Master, look at that!

17:19.955 --> 17:21.582
We found what we were looking for.

17:23.625 --> 17:25.127
-Let's go!
-Yes!

17:25.210 --> 17:27.546
What a powerful Villain.

17:27.629 --> 17:28.881
It's because

17:29.465 --> 17:32.843
of a dangerous drug called Trigger
that turns regular people into Villains.

17:33.594 --> 17:37.014
<i>Those guys are trying to prevent</i>
<i>that drug from being circulated.</i>

17:37.097 --> 17:38.974
They're working as volunteers.

17:42.186 --> 17:45.522
I'm a superhuman. But you guys
are nothing but ordinary humans.

17:45.606 --> 17:48.859
It's useless for you guys to be
scurrying around my feet.

17:53.030 --> 17:54.865
While you're distracted with me…

17:55.908 --> 17:57.618
Off-the-cuff Villains like you

17:58.160 --> 18:00.788
aren't used to handling
your enhanced Quirks yet!

18:01.872 --> 18:03.040
You're so vulnerable!

18:03.749 --> 18:06.293
For example, your Hardening Quirk
hardened the surface

18:06.376 --> 18:09.588
of your body so excessively
that your movements are slow.

18:10.089 --> 18:11.256
Which causes you to stumble.

18:11.340 --> 18:13.258
If you weren't born
with this special ability,

18:13.342 --> 18:15.552
and you have to consciously
activate the "Hardening,"

18:15.636 --> 18:17.930
you'll become soft once you lose focus.

18:18.514 --> 18:20.849
As long as I can get in one hit,
the rest is easy.

18:20.933 --> 18:23.727
I won't give you a chance to recover!

18:28.315 --> 18:32.277
It's because you got carried away
with your hastily made armor, you fool.

18:32.820 --> 18:34.530
You've gone too far!

18:37.074 --> 18:40.452
Look, he lost consciousness,
so his Hardening is losing effect.

18:40.536 --> 18:42.621
Let's take a picture of him
and find out who he is.

18:42.704 --> 18:43.747
Okay.

18:46.792 --> 18:49.002
I can't tell what he looks like.

18:49.670 --> 18:51.213
You beat him up too much.

18:54.633 --> 18:57.094
Thank you so much!

18:57.177 --> 18:58.512
Our pleasure.

18:58.595 --> 19:00.139
Glad you're safe.

19:01.849 --> 19:02.766
All right.

19:03.600 --> 19:06.311
Should we take a picture of him
just in case?

19:06.395 --> 19:08.814
Yeah, and get a picture of his tongue too.

19:08.897 --> 19:09.773
Tongue?

19:10.357 --> 19:14.319
When people use Trigger,
it turns their tongues black.

19:15.612 --> 19:17.197
That proves that they're users.

19:17.781 --> 19:20.951
You guys should make sure
your friends aren't using that drug.

19:21.743 --> 19:23.704
If anything happens, contact me.

19:24.913 --> 19:26.623
Drugs are bad.

19:26.707 --> 19:28.375
Yeah, it's dangerous.

19:29.376 --> 19:30.586
The police are here.

19:30.669 --> 19:31.587
Okay, let's go.

19:34.298 --> 19:36.300
See you next time.

19:39.678 --> 19:42.431
-Hey!
-Come see my live performance!

19:44.183 --> 19:46.310
Who are you guys?

19:47.394 --> 19:49.438
We're the mysterious new Heroes.

19:50.856 --> 19:53.483
Knuckleduster and The Crawler.

20:01.491 --> 20:03.076
Have you identified the suspect?

20:03.160 --> 20:05.412
No matches found on the Villain list.

20:05.495 --> 20:08.373
We're searching for him
in the general Quirk registry now.

20:09.625 --> 20:11.293
<i>According to the local police, the suspect</i>

20:11.376 --> 20:15.839
<i>exhibited superhuman strength and both</i>
<i>Gigantification and Hardening Quirks.</i>

20:15.923 --> 20:17.633
<i>He's the flashy type.</i>

20:18.383 --> 20:20.510
Yes, I'm sure we'll get a hit soon enough.

20:20.594 --> 20:22.679
After all, combined Quirks like this
are rare.

20:23.680 --> 20:27.643
No, I don't think we'll get a hit
from the list we have on file.

20:27.726 --> 20:29.478
What do you mean?

20:31.396 --> 20:34.608
Discoloration of the oral cavity
due to blood flow obstruction

20:34.691 --> 20:36.151
and Quirk enhancement.

20:36.735 --> 20:38.904
It's the side effect
of using Ideo Trigger.

20:39.446 --> 20:41.990
He's what we call an Instant Villain.

20:43.450 --> 20:48.163
But he sure got a beating to his face.
Which Hero made this arrest?

20:48.247 --> 20:50.582
Whoever it is can get suspended
for excessive violence.

20:50.666 --> 20:51.959
Well, about that…

20:52.584 --> 20:56.838
Witnesses told us, "A team of two Heroes
fought against the Villain."

20:56.922 --> 21:00.300
But there are no reports of Heroes
being dispatched to this area.

21:00.884 --> 21:02.261
I see.

21:02.344 --> 21:05.764
It's the same as what happened with
the Gigantification Villain the other day.

21:06.890 --> 21:08.850
Unapproved Illegal Heroes.

21:09.476 --> 21:11.395
It's the work of the Vigilantes.

21:12.145 --> 21:15.274
Well, whoever they are,
it's all's well that ends well,

21:15.357 --> 21:16.692
as long as they defeat the Villains.

21:16.775 --> 21:19.903
Whoa Sansa, stop saying things like that.

21:19.987 --> 21:21.530
Yes, sir.

21:22.114 --> 21:23.699
A thing called the law exists.

21:24.241 --> 21:26.618
Whether the opponent
is a Villain or whatever,

21:27.202 --> 21:30.038
taking it upon yourself
to lynch someone is a crime.

21:34.001 --> 21:36.545
People are talking about today's incident.

21:37.963 --> 21:39.464
What are they saying about the new Heroes?

21:41.341 --> 21:42.509
Everyone is calling you guys

21:43.218 --> 21:44.970
"Monster Fist Geezer"

21:45.554 --> 21:47.180
and "The Squalor".

21:49.641 --> 21:51.476
I'm The Crawler!

21:52.060 --> 21:54.646
I'm The Crawler!

21:54.730 --> 21:55.981
HE SURE LOOKS LIKE A SQUALOR
HE'S REALLY CRAZY

23:26.863 --> 23:29.449
<i>Even though I started working</i>
<i>as an Illegal Hero,</i>

23:29.533 --> 23:31.493
<i>I'm just a humble university student.</i>

23:31.576 --> 23:33.829
<i>More precisely,</i>
<i>a lonely university student.</i>

23:33.912 --> 23:35.247
<i>But there are cases</i>

23:35.330 --> 23:36.873
<i>that I can find because of who I am.</i>

23:37.457 --> 23:40.502
<i>Next episode, "Bee".</i>
<i>I sense something secretive going on.</i>

23:40.585 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
